From: Codex-Android-DevOPS
 <slock-android+codex-android-devops@agents.stamp.build>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:15:49 +0000
Subject: fix(compose): apply a shrinking reverse re-anchor immediately during
 a fling
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The scroll-end deferral of reverse re-anchoring (task #37) also deferred a
shrinking content size. When a short thread's last item becomes visible the
3000dp placeholder is replaced by the exact size; keeping the old, larger
frame let the native fling continue into a region with no items. Device
probe on botiverse/mobile alpha 10020008: placed rows fixed at 28 while the
uncovered viewport grew 0 -> 676px over ~650ms at normal frame cadence, then
contentH 9000 -> 4363 and a jump at scroll end. Only a growing frame, the
case the deferral exists for, still waits for scroll end.

Fork-Patch: compose-reverse-lazy-shrink-reanchor-immediate
Origin: botiverse/mobile task #37 (fast-fling blank rows in thread)
Upstream-Status: pending
Signed-off-by: Codex-Android-DevOPS (林舟) <slock-android+codex-android-devops@agents.stamp.build>

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/compose/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/tencent/kuikly/compose/gestures/ReverseScrollOffsetMapping.kt b/compose/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/tencent/kuikly/compose/gestures/ReverseScrollOffsetMapping.kt
index a37a4711e635c22e6a24d44f9ae650d4feec263e..456b79eaec5464fc77f601072ea860ef16a1ca84 100644
--- a/compose/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/tencent/kuikly/compose/gestures/ReverseScrollOffsetMapping.kt
+++ b/compose/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/tencent/kuikly/compose/gestures/ReverseScrollOffsetMapping.kt
@@ -137,6 +137,12 @@ internal object ReverseScrollOffsetMapping {
      * while the reported native offset stays inside the anchored range: outside it the
      * stale frame no longer describes the position (native already scrolled into the
      * newly grown region, or an overscroll bounce), and the re-anchor must apply now.
+     *
+     * Only a growing content size ([nativeDelta] > 0) defers. A shrinking one means the
+     * estimate overshot the real content (typically the last item just became visible and
+     * the exact size replaced the placeholder): keeping the old, larger frame lets the
+     * native fling run on into a region that has no items, which shows as blank rows that
+     * grow until scroll end and then a jump. That correction applies at once.
      */
     fun shouldDeferReanchor(
         nativeDelta: Int,
@@ -145,7 +151,7 @@ internal object ReverseScrollOffsetMapping {
         anchoredMaxNativeOffset: Int,
         epsilon: Float,
     ): Boolean =
-        !force && nativeDelta != 0 &&
+        !force && nativeDelta > 0 &&
             reportedNativeOffset >= -epsilon &&
             reportedNativeOffset <= anchoredMaxNativeOffset + epsilon
 
